  "raw": {
    "https://www.udmercy.edu/faculty-staff/index.php": {
      "title": "Faculty, Staff and Administrators",
      "description": "Faculty & Staff | University of Detroit Mercy Menu Search Academics Admission & Aid Student Life About Giving Apply Give Students Alumni Faculty/Staff Parents GO Faculty, Staff and Administrators Navigate this Section UDM Home Page Facilities Human Resources IT Services Marketing & Communications Procurement Services Shared Governance Students of Concern Faculty & Staff Employee Emergency Fund Tuition Exchange Programs and FACHEX Home Faculty & Staff Tools and Resources Workplace Tools Office 365 My Portal MS Teams IT Helpdesk Cascade Wellness and Well-being Faculty Resources Blackboard Anthology - Campus Labs Libraries Shared Governance Faculty Handbook Academic Affairs CETL Faculty Advising Faculty/Staff Announcements from Campus Connection Open All | Close All September 08: UDM student organizations to be showcased at Titan Fest, Sept. 11 Tuesday September 08, 2026 The annual student involvement fair, Titan Fest, returns to the McNichols Campus on Sept. 11 at 3 p.m . Held around the Fisher Fountain, Titan Fest is the best spot for students who are interested in joining a student organization to learn about their options at UDM. This year’s event will showcase all returning student organizations, student-facing campus resources, delicious carnival style food, contests and more. For those who are interested in having a table at Titan Fest but are not representing a student organization, email Assistant Director of Student Life Emily Johnson at johnsoem6@udmercy.edu to make a request. September 08: Course Program of Study open forum set for Sept. 16 Tuesday September 08, 2026 An open forum on Course Program of Study (CPoS) is set for Tuesday, Sept. 16 from 12:50-1:50 p.m. inside of the Engineering Building, Room 220. Over the past few months, faculty have received updates about Course Program of Study and its implications for financial aid and enrollment status compliance, including potential impacts on advising. Because this has raised many questions, an open forum is being held during the open hour to address them directly. The session will begin with a brief recap of what CPoS is and why it exists, with the majority of the time reserved for questions from attendees. Faculty and staff who went to ensure a specific question is covered are encouraged to email it in advance to courseeligibility@udmercy.edu , though questions are also welcomed at the session itself. All are welcome. Thank you for your continued support of students through this transition. September 08: Community prayer service for healing and wellness set for Sept. 10 Tuesday September 08, 2026 The Detroit Mercy community is invited to a special prayer service focused on the health and well‑being of local neighborhoods. This gathering offers an opportunity to come together to pause, share space and lift one another up through prayer and reflection. The prayer service will take place on Thursday, Sept. 10, at 6 p.m. , at Good Shepard Lutheran Church, located at 16100 Lawton Street in Detroit. Following the service, attendees are invited to remain for conversation and a shared meal. This is an opportunity to connect, meet new neighbors and build community in a welcoming, relaxed setting. Dinner will be provided through the generosity of the Catholic Foundation of Michigan. All are welcome, whether familiar with prayer services or attending for the first time. The evening is sponsored by Good Shepard Lutheran Church, Titan Equity Nourish Network (TENN) and University Ministry . September 08: Volunteer for ‘Thank a Donor Day’ on Tuesday, Sept. 22 Tuesday September 08, 2026 Students, looking for volunteering opportunities? Hand out prizes, help students with thank-you notes, run game stations, assist with thank you photos and videos, and more during ‘Thank a Donor Day,’ set for 12:30-2 p.m. Tuesday, Sept. 22 in the Fountain Lounge of the Student Union. If you need volunteer hours as part of service requirements for your organizations, there is an opportunity to help out with the annual day on the McNichols Campus. The Annual Giving and Alumni Relations departments host the ‘Thank a Donor Day’ and will have several opportunities to volunteer. To learn more about the various opportunities and times available for you to fulfill your required hours, visit the link below! Volunteer at ‘Thank a Donor Day.’ September 08: Celebrate Spirit! launches new school year, Sept. 17 Tuesday September 08, 2026 Celebrate Spirit! is the official kickoff to the new academic year and a University-wide celebration that welcomes our entire community of students, staff, faculty and administrators. The celebration is set for Thursday, Sept. 17 in the Whitty Student Fitness Center. The 150th Jubilee Mass of the Holy Spirit begins at 11:30 a.m. The celebration includes a Catholic Mass, and individuals from all faith traditions are warmly invited to participate or observe in a manner that feels comfortable to them. Celebrate Spirit! will be presided over by Archbishop Gabriele Giordano Caccia, STD, JCL, the Apostolic Nuncio (Vatican Ambassador) and Pope Leo XIV’s envoy to the United States. The event is hosted by University Ministry and Mission Integration. All are invited to wear red, orange or yellow as part of the event. A lunch and reception will be provided in the Fountain Lounge & Terrace of the Student Union at 1 p.m. Celebrate Spirit! is open to all members of the Detroit Mercy community no matter their religious affiliation. Click here to volunteer at Celebrate Spirit! Celebrate Spirit! 2026 invites the Detroit Mercy community to reflect on “Faith In Action” as this academic year’s theme as part of our 150th Celebration. Faith is not stagnant—it is active. It is not an individual proclamation or checklist—it is something that exists in community and in relationship. Just as God animates our lives, we are called to actively respond to God in all things. This active faith moves us to imagine a prophetic future for our community. In our Ignatian and Mercy traditions, faith-in-action requires discernment and imagination—Where are we headed? Where does the world call us to be? Learn more about Celebrate Spirit! September 08: Titans of Detroit returns Sept. 18 to support Titan Athletics Tuesday September 08, 2026 The second annual Titans of Detroit fundraiser will take place on Friday, Sept. 18 , at the Cambria Hotel Detroit, located at 600 W. Lafayette Blvd. Celebrate Titan Athletics alongside coach Mark Montgomery, coach Kiefer Haffey and special guests at an evening benefiting Detroit Mercy athletic programs. The evening begins with a special reception for VIPs at 5:30 p.m., followed by happy hour at 6 p.m. and then dinner at 7 p.m. in the hotel ballroom. Guests will enjoy complimentary drinks, fine dining and the opportunity to bid on exclusive auction items. Last year, the event brought together more than 250 UDM supporters and raised more than $110,000 for the University’s athletics programs. Featured guests of this year’s celebration include two-time NBA champion and Hall of Famer Isiah Thomas, who will give the keynote presentation, Hall of Fame coach Tom Izzo, NBA All-Star Derrick Coleman, Titan legend John Long, Detroit Mercy coaches and other distinguished members of the athletics community. Tickets are $400 per person, and complimentary valet parking is included courtesy of Cambria Hotel Detroit. Those interested in table sponsorships may contact Jason Clark at 313-682-3295 or clarkje2@udmercy.edu . Guests planning an overnight stay can receive a special hotel discount by calling 313-733-0300 and requesting the Detroit Mercy rate. Limited tickets are available, so register today. Register for Titans of Detroit here. September 08: Take part in Magnetic Poetry Contest in the Briggs Building Tuesday September 08, 2026 All Detroit Mercy students, alumni, staff, faculty and administrators are encouraged to create an original poem using the magnets on the second-floor lockers of the Briggs Building on the McNichols Campus. Winning poems will be published in the 34th issue of [sic], UDM’s arts and literary magazine. Students will also receive a magnetic poetry kit. Each individual may submit a maximum of three poems. Photos of the poems must be high quality and vertically oriented. The deadline is Saturday, Sept. 26 . With any questions or for more information, please contact Director of Creative Writing Stacy Gnall at gnallsc@udmercy.edu . Submit here. Thumbs Up Thursday September 03, 2026 McAuley School of Nursing Professor Andrea Kwasky was elected president-elect of the American Psychiatric Nurses Association, the largest professional organization representing psychiatric-mental health nurses in the United States.\nKwasky will go on to serve as APNA president, bringing more than two decades of experience in psychiatric-mental health nursing, education and mental health advocacy to the role. Find more Thumbs Up Campus Connection Get assistance for providing students with online instruction Instruction for Online Class Delivery The Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning (CETL) is available to assist any Detroit Mercy faculty who would like assistance providing their students with online instruction. This assistance can be provided face-to-face or online. For more information, contact CETL at 313-578-0580. If you have specific questions you may contact: McNichols Campus: Russ Davidson 313-993-1129 or davidsor@udmercy.edu School of Law: Chris Congdon, 313-596-9835 or congdorc@udmercy.edu School of Dentistry: Thomas Zielonka, 313-494-6828 or zielontw@udmercy.edu Employee Directory Students of Concern Students of Concern (Academically) Students of Concern (Student Life) Human Resources and Benefits Benefits Tuition Exchange Programs and FACHEX Employment Opportunities HR Payroll, Forms Policies 3-year Holiday Calendar Visit Human Resources Events, Facilities, Purchasing Event Request (Host event, calendar request ) Facilities Work Request Mail Procurement Visit Facilities Marketing and Fundraising Help Logos, Templates, Letterhead Print Communication | Style or Brand Review Change to a Web Page Submit Story Ideas Update your Biography | Become a Media Expert Campus Announcement | Digital Signage Partner with Annual Giving for Fundraising Teaching Center for Excellence in Teaching & Learning National Center for Faculty Development and Diversity Academic Early Alert Form Placement Testing Faculty Advising Faculty Evaluations Office of Title IX Disability Support Services Schedules and registration Academic Calendar (pdf) Catalogs Class Schedules Office of the Registrar Forms Core Curriculum Requirements My Portal (Registration) Anthology Toolsets Course Evaluations - Evaluate teaching and learning Planning - Connect and manage your strategic planning efforts Faculty - Manage course rosters, faculty evaluations, dashboard Research Corporate and Foundation Relations Office of Academic Affairs Office of Institutional Research OSPRA Office of Mission Integration The Office of Mission Integration is charged with nourishing employee conversations about the soul of the University. MORE ON MISSION Printer-friendly Info for Future Students Current Students Alumni Community Members Faculty & Staff FOLLOW DETROIT MERCY UDM Facebook UDM Twitter UDM YouTube UDM Instagram UDM TikTok UDM LinkedIn University of Detroit Mercy, a Catholic university in the Jesuit and Mercy traditions 4001 W. McNichols Road Detroit, Michigan 48221-3038 CAMPUSES • CONTACT UDM Athletics Mission Public Safety Web Privacy & Policy Consumer Disclosure Careers at UDM Back to Top"
